236:where ``$\circ$'' denotes the entry-wise product and $\vec{f_i}:= F \vec{e_i}$. To verify that the projectors $v_i$ give a valid quantum $d$-coloring, we need to check the completeness and orthogonality conditions,~\EqRef{Complete} and \EqRef{Adj}, from \Def{Qchrom}. The completeness condition $\sum_i v_i = I$, follows directly from the fact that the columns $\vec{r_{vi}}$ of the unitary $U_v$ form an orthonormal basis. To check the orthogonality condition, we need to show that $\tr(v_iw_i) =0 $ for all $i\in[d]$ and all adjacent vertices $v$ and $w$. Since $\tr(v_i w_i) = \abs[\big]{\vec{r_{vi}}\ct \vec{r_{wi}}}^2$, it suffices to check that the vectors $\vec{r_{vi}}$ and $\vec{r_{wi}}$ are orthogonal:
