codex
Outcome: rejected rather than shipping a misleading generator.

The [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1801.03542) shows that:

- Section 3’s projector witnesses come from explicit Fourier or quaternion formulas. Under the 256-atom cap, the mechanical and compact routes have comparable cost; a compressed kernel would merely be a fixed lookup.
- Theorem 1 concerns one fixed graph, while its Gröbner certificate was unavailable and even the smaller `K4` certificate exceeded 7,000 monomials.
- A Section 5 Track-B prototype was viable and passed every local gate, but the no-tool oracles solved every completed difficulty level: 8 verified solves in 15 attempts across five levels.
- OpenRouter then returned account-limit HTTP 403 errors. These were preserved and were not counted as hardness evidence.

